      "content": "thanks for that. it's a solid start but i think the length score is going to be a bit low for our library standards. the system is flagging it as \"brief\" compared to the other modules.\n\ncould you expand on this significantly? try to go into more detail regarding the mathematical derivation or the physical implications (like the wave packet perspective), just so the score is higher. \n\nand again, please be careful—i really don't want \"filler\" or circular logic. i just want a more comprehensive, deep dive that genuinely explains the \"why\" behind the principle so it hits that higher length threshold naturally. thanks!",
